# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 150-152 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 15 — CHAPTERS 17-18, LEAN, 2026-09-24): two witnesses for every capital case, one witness and
# one disciple silent for the prosecution (150); the witnesses' hand first, then any man, the doers of evil purged (151); the hard case — the brilliant judge,
# counsel, the law, the judgment, the three bloods, the three judgments, the three plagues, the valuations, the three rites of contention, the poor man's
# gifts, rise at once and in court, THE THREE COURTS and the Chamber of Hewn Stone from which Torah goes out, the land and the House higher than all (152).
# Every row READ WHOLE in both files; the cuts by ch17_ink.SP_. Sitting 14's form.
from ch17_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(150, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"BY THE MOUTH OF TWO WITNESSES OR THREE WITNESSES SHALL THE DEAD DIE" (17:6) — ONLY THIS ONE? WHENCE ALL THE OTHERS PUT TO DEATH? THE TEACHING SAYS THE VERSE AGAIN. The head row of piska 150 ({SP_(150, 1, "מנין", "לרבות", "שאר", "המומתים")} "whence to include the rest of those put to death"): THE TWO WITNESSES A RULE FOR EVERY CAPITAL CASE, not the idolater\'s alone — "the dead" the general noun (Sifrei Numbers 161 the twin at 35:30): the compile\'s evidence parameter on every death verdict. Fresh.')
srow(150, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE THAT ONE WITNESS DOES NOT ARGUE FOR GUILT? "HE SHALL NOT DIE BY THE MOUTH OF ONE WITNESS". ({SP_(150, 2, "שלא", "ילמד", "עד", "אחד", "חובה")} "that one witness does not argue for guilt"): the single witness barred from the PROSECUTION\'S SIDE — the verse\'s second clause a rule of speech in court, not only of proof. Fresh.')
srow(150, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE THAT A DISCIPLE DOES NOT ARGUE FOR GUILT? "HE SHALL NOT DIE BY THE MOUTH OF ONE WITNESS". ({SP_(150, 3, "שלא", "ילמד", "תלמיד", "חובה")} "that a disciple does not argue for guilt"): the disciple sitting before the court may argue for acquittal, never for guilt (Sanhedrin 5:4 the sheet; the English\'s note: absent from many versions) — the capital court\'s asymmetry, 144:12\'s "justice, justice" in the seats. Fresh.')
srow(151, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE HAND OF THE WITNESSES SHALL BE ON HIM FIRST TO PUT HIM TO DEATH" (17:7) — A COMMANDMENT ON THE WITNESSES TO PUT HIM TO DEATH. The head row of piska 151 ({SP_(151, 1, "מצוה", "בעדים", "להמיתו")} "a commandment on the witnesses to put him to death"): THE WITNESSES EXECUTE — the duty theirs (Sifrei Numbers 114 the twin; 13:10\'s "your hand first" the brother\'s): the compile\'s execution effect keyed on the witnesses as actors. Fresh.')
srow(151, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE THAT IF HE DID NOT DIE BY THE WITNESSES\' HAND HE DIES BY ANY MAN\'S? "AND THE HAND OF ALL THE PEOPLE AFTERWARD". ({SP_(151, 2, "ימות", "ביד", "כל", "אדם")} "let him die by the hand of any man"): the second clause the fallback (Sanhedrin 6:4) — the compile\'s execution in two stages, 306:9\'s image of Heaven\'s retributions built on it (REREAD there). Fresh.')
srow(151, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL PURGE THE EVIL FROM YOUR MIDST" — PURGE THE DOERS OF EVIL FROM ISRAEL. ({SP_(151, 3, "בער", "עושי", "הרעות", "מישראל")} "purge the doers of evil from Israel"): THE PURGE FORMULA at its second seat of nine (asserted) read as PERSONS, not an abstraction — and ONKELOS WRITES THE SAME ("the doer of evil" at every purge seat, asserted): the compile\'s purge effect a removal from the population ledger (13:6 its first seat, chapter 13\'s cell reused). Fresh.')
srow(152, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN A MATTER IS TOO HARD FOR YOU" (17:8) — TEACHES THAT THE VERSE SPEAKS OF THE DISTINGUISHED ONE. The head row of piska 152 ({SP_(152, 1, "שבמפלא", "הכתוב", "מדבר")} "that the verse speaks of the distinguished one"): "too hard" (the root of "wonder") read as the court\'s DISTINGUISHED JUDGE (the mufla of the court, Horayot 1:4 the English\'s note) — the verse re-signified to the court\'s own office: the compile\'s high court a body with a named head. Fresh.')
srow(152, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"FROM YOU" — THIS IS COUNSEL. ({SP_(152, 2, "ממך", "זו", "עצה")} "from you — this is counsel"): the first of the verse\'s words made a category of the hard case. Fresh.')
srow(152, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"A MATTER" — THIS IS THE LAW — halakha (the law). ({SP_(152, 3, "דבר", "זו", "הלכה")} "a matter — this is the law"): the oral law\'s own word given the verse\'s "matter" — the second category. Fresh.')
srow(152, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR JUDGMENT" — THIS IS THE VERDICT. ({SP_(152, 4, "למשפט", "זה", "הדין")} "for judgment — this is the verdict"): the third — the case decided: counsel, law, verdict the three grades of the question the compile\'s high court takes. Fresh.')
srow(152, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"BETWEEN BLOOD AND BLOOD" — BETWEEN THE BLOOD OF MENSTRUATION, OF CHILDBIRTH, OF DISCHARGE. ({SP_(152, 5, "בין", "דם", "נדה", "לדם", "יולדת", "לדם", "זיבה")} "between the blood of the menstruant, the blood of the woman in childbirth, the blood of discharge"): THE THREE BLOODS the women\'s laws of Leviticus 12 and 15 (the run\'s ledgers), not homicide — the shelf\'s reading of the pair; "between blood and blood" two seats in the Bible (here and Jehoshaphat\'s 2 Chronicles 19:10, asserted). Fresh.')
srow(152, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"BETWEEN PLEA AND PLEA" — BETWEEN MONEY CASES, CAPITAL CASES, CASES OF LASHES. ({SP_(152, 6, "בין", "דיני", "ממונות", "לדיני", "נפשות", "לדיני", "מכות")} "between money cases, capital cases and cases of lashes"): THE THREE JUDGMENTS — Sanhedrin 1\'s three courts of three, twenty-three, twenty-three (the answer sheet; 14b\'s tiers parameter) hung on the second pair. Fresh.')
srow(152, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"BETWEEN STROKE AND STROKE" — BETWEEN THE PLAGUES OF MEN, OF GARMENTS, OF HOUSES. ({SP_(152, 7, "בין", "נגעי", "אדם", "לנגעי", "בגדים", "לנגעי", "בתים")} "between the plagues of men, of garments, of houses"): THE THREE PLAGUES Leviticus 13-14\'s three (the run\'s ledgers) — Onkelos writes "the plague of confinement" (asserted, three seats): the third pair. Fresh.')
srow(152, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"MATTERS OF" — THESE ARE VALUATIONS, DEVOTIONS AND CONSECRATIONS. ({SP_(152, 8, "אלו", "ערכים", "וחרמים", "והקדשות")} "these are valuations, devotions and consecrations"): Leviticus 27\'s three (the run\'s ledger lev_27) read out of the construct "matters of" — a fourth category before the pair "contention". Fresh.')
srow(152, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"CONTENTION" — THIS IS THE SOTAH\'S DRAUGHT, THE HEIFER\'S NECK, THE LEPER\'S CLEANSING. ({SP_(152, 9, "השקית", "סוטה", "ועריפת", "עגלה", "וטהרת", "מצורע")} "the sotah\'s draught, the heifer\'s neck-breaking and the leper\'s cleansing"): THREE RITES the high court\'s business (Numbers 5, 21:1-9 ahead, Leviticus 14 — the run\'s ledgers): the priests\' rites the court adjudicates. Fresh.')
srow(152, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"IN YOUR GATES" — THIS IS GLEANING, THE FORGOTTEN SHEAF AND THE CORNER. ({SP_(152, 10, "זה", "לקט", "שכחה", "ופאה")} "this is gleaning, the forgotten sheaf and the corner"): the poor man\'s three gifts (Leviticus 19:9-10, 24:19 ahead) the "gates" — the field\'s laws in the local court: the compile\'s local tier keeps the agricultural gifts. Fresh.')
srow(152, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL RISE" — AT ONCE. ({SP_(152, 11, "וקמת", "מיד")} "and you shall rise — at once"): the rising immediate — a clock on the referral. Fresh.')
srow(152, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL RISE" — IN COURT. ({SP_(152, 12, "וקמת", "בבית", "דין")} "and you shall rise — in court"): the rising from the LOCAL court — the referral a court\'s act, not a litigant\'s: the compile\'s referral effect from the lower tier. Fresh.')
srow(152, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'FROM HERE THEY SAID (MISHNAH SANHEDRIN 11:2): THREE COURTS WERE THERE — ONE AT THE ENTRANCE OF THE TEMPLE MOUNT, ONE AT THE ENTRANCE OF THE COURTYARD, ONE IN THE CHAMBER OF HEWN STONE. ({SP_(152, 13, "שלשה", "בתי", "דינים", "היו", "שם")} "three courts were there"; {SP_(152, 13, "ואחד", "בלשכת", "הגזית")} "and one in the Chamber of Hewn Stone"): THE MISHNAH CITED IN THE HEBREW ITSELF (the row without a verse citation) — THE THREE COURTS AT THE PLACE, the tiers\' seats: the compile\'s high court three bodies at three gates (the 14b courts daemon\'s owed second half). Fresh.')
srow(152, 14, 'MATERIAL', f'THEY COME TO THE ONE AT THE TEMPLE MOUNT\'S GATE AND HE SAYS "THUS I EXPOUNDED AND THUS MY FELLOWS, THUS I TAUGHT AND THUS MY FELLOWS"; IF THEY HAVE HEARD, THEY TELL THEM; IF NOT, TO THE ONE AT THE COURTYARD\'S ENTRANCE; IF NOT, BOTH COME TO THE GREAT COURT IN THE CHAMBER OF HEWN STONE, FROM WHICH TORAH GOES OUT TO ALL ISRAEL, AS IT IS SAID "FROM THAT PLACE WHICH THE LORD WILL CHOOSE" (17:10). ({SP_(152, 14, "כך", "דרשתי", "וכך", "דרשו", "חברי")} "thus I expounded and thus my fellows expounded"; {SP_(152, 14, "שמשם", "תורה", "יוצאה", "לכל", "ישראל")} "for from there Torah goes out to all Israel"): THE APPEAL\'S PROTOCOL in three stations with the formula spoken at each (Sanhedrin 11:2, Tosefta Sanhedrin 7:1) — "if they have heard" a TRADITION lookup, the great court the source when none exists: the compile\'s escalation a three-step function returning either a heard ruling or the great court\'s new one; "from that place" the verse\'s own seat. Fresh.')
srow(152, 15, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL RISE AND GO UP" — TEACHES THAT THE LAND OF ISRAEL IS HIGHER THAN ALL LANDS AND THE TEMPLE HIGHER THAN ALL THE LAND. ({SP_(152, 15, "מגיד", "שארץ", "ישראל", "גבוהה", "מכל", "הארצות")} "teaches that the land of Israel is higher than all the lands"): "go UP" read as height — 37:16, 317:2 and 352:9 all cite this verse for the same teaching (REREAD/fresh there): the place\'s elevation a stated property of the tape\'s land. Fresh.')
